WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.438 --> 00:00:02.281
"Only God can forgive sins.

2
00:00:02.281 --> 00:00:06.101
Why tell a priest?" Catholics agree with the first half.

3
00:00:06.101 --> 00:00:10.263
The Catechism says it in three words: only God forgives sins.

4
00:00:10.713 --> 00:00:12.623
But look at what Jesus does.

5
00:00:12.623 --> 00:00:15.011
In Mark chapter two, people object,

6
00:00:15.011 --> 00:00:22.857
"who can forgive sins but God alone?" And Jesus answers that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins.

7
00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:26.377
Then on Easter night, in John chapter twenty,

8
00:00:26.377 --> 00:00:31.017
he breathes on the apostles and says: "Whose sins you shall forgive,

9
00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:34.838
they are forgiven them; and whose sins you shall retain,

10
00:00:34.838 --> 00:00:39.750
they are retained." You can't forgive or retain what you've never heard.

11
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.547
That's why confession is spoken out loud.

12
00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:45.385
So the priest isn't a rival to God.

13
00:00:45.385 --> 00:00:47.364
He's what Jesus chose to use,

14
00:00:47.364 --> 00:00:51.662
the way he chose water for baptism and bread for the Eucharist.

15
00:00:51.662 --> 00:00:52.549
God forgives.

16
00:00:52.549 --> 00:00:55.414
The priest says the words Christ gave him.

17
00:00:55.864 --> 00:00:57.638
And there's one more gift.

18
00:00:57.638 --> 00:01:00.845
You get to hear it, out loud: you are forgiven.
